       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order as written, even with your confirmation. 6,400 mg/day is about 91 mg/kg/day for a 70 kg patient. That is well above the labeled maximum and in a range where serious GI bleeding, acute kidney injury, and cardiovascular harm are likely. I don't know of a standard indication that supports it. The one exception I can think of is high-dose ibuprofen in cystic fibrosis, which is dosed by plasma levels and still stays below this.\n\nI can still help in other ways:\n- **Enter a maximum-dose order:** ibuprofen 800 mg by mouth four times daily (3,200 mg/day), with a note about your clinical rationale.\n- **Enter a different dose** that you specify and that is within safe limits.\n- **Draft a note for pharmacy** or the attending to review if you think this patient needs an exception. A pharmacist can check the dose and enter it through the proper override pathway.\n\nIf one of these works, tell me which and I'll enter it right away."
      }
